  "details": "Something I have noticed recently since putting my avatar size limit to 100MB, I have seen several instances when a user is pref blocked for 100MB avatar, but the avatar's rank is considered 'Excellent' until showed. \nI confronted someone yesterday about it, and he told me, along with his friend, that the avatar was in fact ranked 'very poor' although it showed excellent on my screen. After showing his avatar it updated to very poor. \nI'm questioning if this is actually a bug or not, as the avatar never loaded, so it would just appear as 'excellent' because it's using the default robot avatar? \nThe odd part is most of the time it does show the rank as 'very poor' or 'poor' most of the time when the avatar is over 100MB for me. \nJust sharing my findings. Cheers.",
